        "name": "USN-8226-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that the Linux kernel algif_aead module contained a logic flaw allowing a local attacker to escalate privileges to root. This update to the kmod package disables loading the algif_aead module as a measure to mitigate the issue until kernel updates are made available.  See the following URL for more information https://ubuntu.com/blog/copy-fail-vulnerability-fixes-available",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-31431"
        ]
